c(35, "§7.1 era table (verbatim); §7.1 year table (verbatim); §7.1 month table (verbatim); §7.1", "timeline", "Eras defined from the corpus and release dates — E1 launch and 'no ads' praise (2023-01-31 → 2024-06-11), E2 ad complaints begin (2024-06-12 → 2025-06-30), E3 no releases, requests pile up (2025-07-01 → 2026-07-15, a calendar split of the 19-month release gap), E4 the 1.2.0 crash wave (2026-07-16 → 07-22), E5 after 1.2.1 (verbatim): " + table("## 7.1 Method", 0) + " || by year (verbatim): " + table("## 7.1 Method", 1) + " || by month (verbatim): " + table("## 7.1 Method", 2) + " — volume grew 5.30 → 13.83 → 19.74 reviews per 30 days, then 295.71 in the crash week and 19.57 after; E1–E3 and E5 means 4.62–4.70★ against E4 2.41★; 2026 mean 4.03★ with 32 one-star (64 crashes) against 4.60–4.71 in earlier years; July 2026 alone 81 reviews at 2.70★ with 42 low-star.", "n/a", "mixed", "E1 88 / 4.62★; E2 177 / 4.64★; E3 250 / 4.66★; E4 69 / 2.41★ / 295.71 per 30d; E5 30 / 4.70★; 2026-07 81 / 2.70★", "none", "table", "app-specific", ["11374484206", "14309392133"], "", "")

c(36, "§7.2 table (verbatim); §7.2 movement table (verbatim); §7.4; §7.5", "timeline", "Theme movement (verbatim): " + table("## 7.2 Theme movement", 0) + " || movements (verbatim): " + table("## 7.2 Theme movement", 1) + " — praise stable except the crash week (85.2% → 87.0% → 82.0% → 24.6% → 83.3%); the crash a one-week event (0 → 0.6 → 0 → 92.8 → 0%); the widget persistent for three and a half years and slowly diluted (19.3% → 6.7%), never built across a 19-month release gap and not added in 1.2.0; tree growth persistent to June 2026; ads negative emerged in 2024 and persisted — ads turned from praise (from 2023-01-31) to complaint (2024-06-12 → 2026-06-20), gambling ads 2025-05 and 2025-09; outcomes rising as users stay longer (14.8% → 26.0% → 30.0%; QUIT_ABSTAINING 4.5% → 10.8% in E3; safety-sensitive 2.3% → 6.0%); maintenance doubts appeared in the release gap (NEGLECT first 2025-07-08); helpful votes go to early requests and crash reports; early signals before E4: a launch crash in September 2024, counter errors tied to the phone clock and attempts (2024-08, 2024-10), a habit that deleted itself (2024-04) and a reset after a week (2025-01).", "n/a", "mixed", "WIDGET 19.3 → 16.4 → 14.4 → 2.9 → 6.7%; ads_negative 0 → 4.5 → 4.8 → 0 → 0%; outcome 14.8 → 17.5 → 26.0 → 0 → 30.0%; CRASH 0 → 0.6 → 0 → 92.8 → 0%", "none", "High-priority", "app-specific", ["14469862599", "11735356386", "11644642764", "11876692458", "11194993574", "12207978135"], "", "")

c(37, "§7.3 table (verbatim); §7.3; §9.H", "timeline", "The crash week by day (verbatim): " + table("## 7.3 The crash week", 0) + " — 69 reviews in seven days (295.71 per 30 days vs 19.74 in E3), 64 crash reports, mean 2.41★, 58.0% one- or two-star; storefronts RU 44, US 15, KZ 3, CA 1, TJ 1; release context 1.2.0 (07-15, 'translated into more languages'), 1.2.1 (07-21, 'Improved application performance'), 1.2.2 (07-30, 'Improved application stability') — timing, not proven cause, but 21 say it started after the update, 14 when the ad or banner loads, 3 that it stops without internet; ads appear to be new in that build ('after ads were added — I don't mind that — the app crashes as soon as the ad starts'); recovery: the fix reported 07-22, one reviewer had promised 'if they fix it I'll change to 5'; after 07-22 30 reviews contain no crash — 'moderate evidence of a fix'. Burst check: the only bursts are the crash week (14 reviews on 07-20 and 07-21); outside it no day exceeds four reviews; no solicitation language; repeated short titles are common phrasing; META_CITES_OTHER_REVIEWS 8 echo tree growth or the widget, likely seeded by the 109-vote review; one claims reviews are bought; 'the corpus's weakness is short text, not manipulation'.", "n/a", "1★-burst", "crash week 69 / 64 crashes / 2.41★; ru 44, us 15; fix in 6 days; post-fix 30 reviews 0 crashes; max 14/day", "none", "High-priority", "app-specific", ["14314195428", "14334098154", "14330378148", "10856120064", "13716590558"], "", "")

c(38, "§8.1", "must-never-break", "§8.1 immediate fix — ads must never be able to take the counter down: BUG_CRASH 65 (64 in one week after 1.2.0), CRASH_AD_LOAD 14, OFFLINE_WORKAROUND 3, 40 of 62 low-star reviews, a reviewer who could not log a relapse and one who feared losing years of notes; initialise the ad SDK after the counter renders, catch and fail open on any ad load error, test release builds with the network on and ads live on current iOS, stage rollouts and watch crash rates by build for the first 48 hours, share the fix across the portfolio since the same crash hit the developer's other app; 'for this audience a crash is not an inconvenience — the counter is the commitment device, and if a relapse happens I can't log it is the product failing at its one job'.", "ad SDK on the launch path", "1★-burst", "CRASH 65 / 10.59%; AD_LOAD 14; OFFLINE 3; low-star 40 of 62", "must-never-break", "High-priority", "generalisable", ["14331606843", "14313036902", "14317387419", "14316886107"], "", "")

c(39, "§8.2", "dont", "§8.2 immediate fix — block gambling, alcohol and tobacco ad categories: ADS_HARMFUL_CONTENT 2 — betting, casinos and gambling ads inside an addiction app, one calling it a scam; U:safety_sensitive 23; enforce category exclusions (gambling, alcohol, tobacco and vaping, dating) at the ad network and verify them per storefront — 'two reports clear no frequency threshold; the harm case does'.", "gambling ads served to addiction-recovery users", "complaint", "HARMFUL_CONTENT 2 / 0.33% (promoted on safety grounds); safety_sensitive 23", "dont", "Weak", "generalisable", ["12635810456", "13174041563"], "", "")

c(40, "§8.3", "tactic", "§8.3 experiment — a home-screen and lock-screen widget: REQ_WIDGET 86 (14.01%) in every era since February 2023, 30 of 87 four-star reviews, the second- and third-most-voted reviews (33 and 32 votes), churn over its absence, one purchase intent conditional on it; ship a free counter widget (habit name, days, circle) and measure retention and daily opens; test premium widget styles inside the ad-free subscription as a separate arm — 'the widget is the product's mechanism — keeping the number visible — so gate styling, not the number'.", "no widget", "request", "WIDGET 86 / 14.01%; 4★ 30 of 87; votes 33 + 32; churn 1; purchase intent 1", "tactic", "High-priority", "generalisable", ["10929591148", "14103004927", "10456809560"], "", "")

c(41, "§8.4", "tactic", "§8.4 experiment — let progress be seen and celebrated: REQ_TREE_GROWTH 28 with the corpus's most-voted review (109 votes), MOTIVATION_CONTENT 14, NOTIFICATIONS 11, a reviewer who forgot the app in three days, and a counter-signal — one finds plain numbers calmer than praise; a tree that grows with the current streak and does not wither on relapse ('relapses are a note, not a punishment'); optional milestone notifications off by default; measure 7- and 30-day retention against the static tree.", "static tree; no milestones; no notifications", "request", "TREE 28 / 4.56% (109 votes); MOTIVATION 14; NOTIFICATIONS 11; counter-signal 1", "tactic", "Very strong", "generalisable", ["10801415396", "13305706545", "13322337199"], "", "")

c(42, "§8.5", "must-have", "§8.5 immediate fix — make goals editable and explain them: goal_setting 25 (4.07%), new users who cannot find where to change 'goal: 1', a 7→30 jump and a 100-year goal, a report that custom goals were removed; show on first run that goals advance automatically, allow a custom next milestone, and use a gentler ladder (1, 3, 7, 14, 30, 60, 90 days, then yearly).", "fixed auto-advancing ladder, unexplained", "request", "goal_setting 25 / 4.07%; STEPS_RIGID 15; HOWTO 13", "must-have", "Very strong", "generalisable", ["12689955719", "12867989318", "10814511549", "13804456581", "14456135031", "13034811450"], "", "")

c(43, "§8.6", "tactic", "§8.6 experiment — lifetime ad removal and a clearer free promise: WANT_ONE_TIME_PURCHASE 2, SUBSCRIPTION_OBJECTION 2, PAYWALL_PERCEIVED 6 (all Russian), PAID_EXPLICIT 2 (both ad removal); add a one-time 'remove ads forever' purchase beside the monthly and yearly plans, and state on the purchase screen that every feature stays free; measure purchase rate and one-star 'paid app' reviews in RU.", "subscription-only ad removal read as a paywall", "blocked-conversion", "WANT_ONE_TIME 2; SUBSCRIPTION_OBJECTION 2; PAYWALL_PERCEIVED 6; PAID 2", "tactic", "Emerging", "generalisable", ["11641762030", "14162589436", "11890941612"], "", "")

c(44, "§8.7; §8.8", "product-rule", "§8.7 immediate fix — design for recovery from self-harm and drugs: USE_SELF_HARM 13, USE_DRUGS 8, USE_TREATMENT_CONTEXT 3, users asking for supportive relapse copy, negative wording noticed ('the words refusal, bad habits, relapse are so-so'); when a habit is self-harm or a drug, show crisis and support resources in the articles and relapse flow for each supported language, use non-judgemental relapse copy, and keep ads out of that flow. §8.8 research: what in 1.2.0 caused the crash (a new ad banner, the localisation update, or both) and why offline use avoided it; which ad categories are served in Russian-speaking storefronts and how often gambling ads appear; whether users want backup or transfer (REQ_BACKUP_SYNC 4) and how that squares with a 'works offline' promise and a tracking privacy label for sensitive habits; whether the perceived paywall is real — an onboarding offer, a trial screen, or a different app.", "relapse flow shows ads; no crisis resources", "mixed", "SELF_HARM 13; DRUGS 8; TREATMENT 3; supportive-copy requests 2; 4 open questions", "product-rule", "Meaningful", "generalisable", ["10995642477", "14118955087", "11848596914", "13609431141", "12780782479"], "", "")

c(45, "§8.9 copy table (verbatim); §8.9 don't table (verbatim); §8.9", "dont", "§8.9 what to copy (verbatim): " + table("## 8.9 What this corpus says to copy", 0) + " || what not to copy (verbatim): " + table("## 8.9 What this corpus says to copy", 1) + " — copy a minimal counter that makes a streak feel costly to break, unlimited habits and a relapse note free, a non-triggering quiet interface; don't let an ad load path crash the app, serve gambling ads in an addiction app, leave the most-requested feature unbuilt for years, or ship a fixed goal ladder users cannot see or change.", "n/a", "mixed", "3 copy; 4 don'ts", "dont", "High-priority", "generalisable", ["10508150052", "12476493945", "12635810456", "14469862599"], "", "")

